<title>GERMANY: Germany's Hesse says planning budget freeze.</title>
<headline>Germany's Hesse says planning budget freeze.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German state of Hesse, home to Germany's financial capital of Frankfurt, said on Wednesday that it was planning a budget freeze in the light of low estimates for tax receipts.</p>
<p>&quot;I gained the approval of the (Hesse) cabinet today to take preventative budgetary measures on the basis of clear figures,&quot; Hesse's finance minister Karl Starzacher said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;At the moment I am assuming that a freeze which may become necessary can be limited until September 30,&quot; he added.</p>
</text>
